From 0b9ecbbc9fafe7097b575664922b3e0e4f4dd866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter0x44 <peter0x44@disroot.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:50:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: translate diagnostic colors for legacy Windows
 consoles

The previous change prevents raw ANSI sequences from reaching legacy
Windows consoles by stripping diagnostic colors. That fixes unreadable
output, but loses colors that the compiler would preserve when writing
directly to the same console.

When colors are enabled and the destination console lacks virtual
terminal processing, replay captured diagnostics through the Windows
console API instead. This gives legacy consoles the same readable,
colored diagnostics available when running the compiler directly, while
leaving redirected output and VT-enabled consoles unchanged.

The translation is based on GCC's MinGW console handling in
gcc/pretty-print.cc.
---
